This testbench covers the following aspects:

1.  The counter resets to 1 when the reset input is high.
2.  The counter counts up to 10, inclusive, when the reset input is low.
3.  The counter increments on the positive edge of the clock.
4.  The counter does not exceed 10 when the reset input is low.

The testbench uses a simple stimulus loop to drive the counter through its expected values. It checks the output of the counter against the expected values using the `!==` operator. If any of the expected values do not match the actual output, the `errors` counter is incremented. After the stimulus loop, the testbench checks if the counter has reached 10. If any checks fail, the testbench prints a failure message and terminates the simulation.

